  "body": "https://github.com/w3c/webdriver-bidi/pull/62 is defining parts of the WebDriver BiDi protocol to enumerate browsing contexts, and events for when browsing contexts are created/destroyed, `browsingContext.contextCreated` and `browsingContext.contextDestroyed`.\r\n\r\nHow to hook in to HTML to do this correctly isn't entirely clear. Presently, there's \"Whenever the X algorithm is invoked\" hooks for these two algorithms:\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/#creating-a-new-browsing-context\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/#a-browsing-context-is-discarded\r\n\r\nHowever, neither of these terms are exported. That could be easily done, but these are algorithms intended to be invoked by HTML only, other specs shouldn't invoke them.\r\n\r\nShould we instead define additional \"browsing context tree change steps\" or something akin to https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#unloading-document-cleanup-steps for this?\r\n\r\n@jgraham",
